From: Michiel <367462+meghuizen@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 23 Sep 2026 10:35:41 +0200
Subject: [PATCH nf-next 0/3] netfilter: conntrack: cheaper tuple hashing, max/buckets warning

This series makes two changes to how conntrack hashes tuples and adds
one diagnostic:

1. IPv4 tuples are hashed with siphash_2u64() over the 16 bytes that
   matter instead of siphash() over 39 bytes.  This runs on every
   conntrack lookup.
2. The unscaled tuple hashes are stored in struct nf_conn at insertion,
   so teardown no longer hashes both tuples again just to choose the
   bucket locks.
3. A warning and a documentation note when nf_conntrack_max is raised
   above 8 times nf_conntrack_buckets, because the table is not resized.

Kernel instructions measured in an x86_64 guest (nested KVM), the
series against the base commit, 2 boots against 7 interleaved base
boots:

  new flow, per packet          16845 -> 16686   (-155, two IPv4 hashes)
  established stream, per pkt   14422 -> 14311   (inside the spread)
  conntrack -F, per entry        1908 ->  1311   (-597, patch 2)

There is no packet-rate or latency measurement.

  #  summary                          impact                  evidence
  1  hash IPv4 tuples as two words    medium: IPv4 conntrack  measured
                                      lookups, per packet     (insn counts)
  2  keep unscaled hashes for         low: per deleted        measured
     teardown                         conntrack entry         (insn counts)
  3  warn when max > 8 x buckets      low: diagnostic         tested

Testing:
- Every commit builds the touched objects (nf_conntrack_core.o,
  nf_conntrack_standalone.o, nf_conntrack_netlink.o, nf_conntrack_bpf.o,
  nf_nat_core.o) with W=1 and no warnings on x86_64.  nf_conntrack_core.o
  also builds on i386.
- checkpatch.pl --strict is clean apart from the missing Signed-off-by.
- Instruction counts per call on x86_64 and i386 (perf stat,
  instructions:u).  Structure layout on both (pahole).
- Generated code, built kernel: the IPv4 path of hash_conntrack_raw()
  calls siphash_2u64() instead of __siphash_unaligned();
  __nf_ct_delete_from_lists() makes no hash call (two before).
- Runtime, x86_64 guest, 2 boots of the series: the counts above;
  ctnetlink insert/delete across a table resize and three resizes during
  flow churn leave the table consistent; the patch 3 warning stays
  silent at 8x and fires once at 9x; no kernel warnings.

Not tested:
- Packet rate and latency; hardware other than a nested KVM guest;
  IPv6 at runtime; i386 at runtime.
- No allyesconfig/allmodconfig builds, no arm64 or RISC-V builds, no
  sparse, no netfilter selftests.
- The series is against v7.3-rc3 (518e5b794c06) and has not been
  rebased onto nf-next.

Tool assistance: the changes, changelogs and measurements in this series
were produced with Claude (Anthropic, claude-opus-5-5) as a coding
assistant.  It was asked to find and fix performance problems in the
networking forwarding path and to measure them.  Each patch carries an
Assisted-by tag.

